### Authentication Gauntlet Lab
### Write REST Client request blocks below each phase header.
### Run a block with Ctrl+Alt+R (Windows/Linux) or Cmd+Alt+R (macOS).
### All endpoints live under http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/
### Do not commit real opaque tokens, JWT access tokens, or refresh tokens.

@baseUrl = http://127.0.0.1:8000


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PHASE 1 — Basic Authentication
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Phase 1 — Basic Auth (unauthenticated)
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/basic/ HTTP/1.1

###

### Phase 1 — Basic Auth (with credentials)
### Base64("admin:admin123") = YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM=
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/basic/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM=

###

### Phase 1 — Basic Auth replay demonstration
### Base64 is encoding, not encryption; a captured header can be replayed.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/basic/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Basic YWRtaW46YWRtaW4xMjM=


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PHASE 3 — Token Authentication (Opaque)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Generate/reset a local test token with:
### python manage.py drf_create_token -r admin
###
### For local testing, replace the placeholders temporarily.
### Before committing, restore these placeholders and never commit a real token.

### Phase 3 — Valid Opaque Token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/token/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Token <YOUR_TOKEN>

###

### Phase 3 — Tampered Token
### Copy the local test token and change only its final character.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/token/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Token <YOUR_TOKEN_WITH_LAST_CHARACTER_CHANGED>

### Expected:
### Valid token request: 200 OK
### Tampered token request: 401 Unauthorized


### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
### PHASE 4 — JSON Web Tokens (JWT)
### ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

### Phase 4 — JWT Login (obtain access and refresh tokens)
POST http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/jwt/login/ HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
    "username": "admin",
    "password": "admin123"
}

###

### After sending the login request, temporarily paste the returned token values below.
### Do not commit actual JWT values.
@accessToken = eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9.eyJ0b2tlbl90eXBlIjoiYWNjZXNzIiwiZXhwIjoxNzkwNDY0NjE1LCJpYXQiOjE3OTA0NjI4MTUsImp0aSI6IjVlMDljMTYzZTBlMjQzOTg4YTcwMGVkY2Q5Zjk2Yjg5IiwidXNlcl9pZCI6IjEifQ.k5hkVrRuwYaBPs1UQ0Fipia_hs56ik3KjGpOzES31DQ
@refreshToken = <REFRESH_TOKEN>

###

### Phase 4 — JWT Protected Request
# Paste your access token below, replacing <ACCESS_TOKEN>
GET http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/jwt/protected/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer {{accessToken}}

###

### Phase 4 — JWT Refresh
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/jwt/refresh/ HTTP/1.1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "refresh": "{{refreshToken}}"
}

###

### Phase 4 — Tampered JWT
### Create this at jwt.io by changing user_id in the payload.
### The server rejects it because editing a signed JWT invalidates its signature.
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/jwt/protected/ HTTP/1.1
Authorization: Bearer <TAMPERED_JWT>

### Expected:
### Tampered JWT request: 401 Unauthorized.
### Reason: changing the payload invalidates the JWT signature.